<meta type=article>
<title | Config-driven contents — body placement (#218)>
<author | The Enscribe Team>
</meta>

<config toc=true toc-depth=2 toc-location=body />

<section #sec:intro | Introduction>

The contents listing is config-driven (`<config toc>`), read in the shared compiler,
so the static build and the live render produce it identically. With
`toc-location=body` it renders at the top of the document, after the title block.

<sub-section | Background>

A second-level heading — listed, because `toc-depth=2` includes levels 1 and 2.

<sub-sub-section | Fine detail>

A third-level heading. Below `toc-depth`, so it is absent from the contents listing
(it still renders here in the body).

<section | Methods>

A first-level heading, listed.

<section +unlisted | Acknowledgements>

An `+unlisted` section: present in the document, absent from the contents listing,
regardless of `toc-depth`.
